.TH PLENS 1 "October 2026" "plens 0.1.0" "PortLens Manual"
.SH NAME
plens \- terminal-only server-exposure auditor for operators who run their own VPS/nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plens
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBPortLens\fR (\fBplens\fR) is a high-speed, defensive server-exposure auditor. Unlike traditional port scanners that only report open socket states, PortLens correlates inside listening processes with remote reachability, executes strictly safe non-destructive verification probes (e.g. unauthenticated Redis, MongoDB, Elasticsearch, Docker API), scores exposure risk (0-100), tracks baseline drift, and generates copy-paste remediation commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBscan\fR [\fITARGETS...\fR]
Execute exposure audit on targets. Supports presets (\fBquick\fR, \fBstandard\fR, \fBfull\fR, \fBstealth\fR, \fBweb\fR, \fBudp\fR) and hosting profiles.
.TP
\fBself\fR
Perform inside-vs-outside visibility audit on the local machine.
.TP
\fBwatch\fR \fITARGET\fR [\fB--every\fR \fIDURATION\fR]
Continuously audit target and highlight only detected changes (rolling diff view).
.TP
\fBfix\fR \fIID\fR
Generate copy-paste remediation commands for firewall and service configuration.
.TP
\fBexplain\fR \fIPORT|SERVICE\fR
Offline plain-language knowledge guidance for common network services.
.TP
\fBdiff\fR \fIA\fR \fIB\fR
Compare two scans or scan against baseline with colored drift indicators.
.TP
\fBbaseline\fR <set|show|clear> \fITARGET\fR
Store and inspect expected host states.
.TP
\fBschedule\fR <add|list|rm|run>
Manage automated recurring background audit jobs.
.TP
\fBdaemon\fR [\fB--install-systemd\fR]
Run scheduler daemon or generate systemd service unit.
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Verify environment health, privileges, socket limits, and database.
.TP
\fBui\fR
Interactive terminal user interface (Ratatui TUI).
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success / clean audit.
.TP
\fB1\fR
General operational error.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Findings exceeded \fB--fail-on\fR threshold or unexpected baseline drift detected.
.TP
\fB3\fR
Required dependency (nmap) is missing.
.TP
\fB4\fR
Target authorization declined or allowlist violation.
.TP
\fB130\fR
Process interrupted (partial results saved).
